        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Heinrich August Marschner, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Carl Maria von Weber\n- Works: Der Vampyr, The Turkish March (Marcia alla turca)\n- Topics: German opera, Turkish style in classical music\n\nFacts:\n- Heinrich August Marschner was the most important composer of German opera between Carl Maria von Weber and the opera Der Vampyr.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart wrote The Turkish March, also known as Marcia alla turca.\n- The Turkish March is a well-known classical march theme written in the Turkish style that was popular in music of its time.",
